From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:00:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] opkg.py: support data.tar.zst, keep stdout clean

oe-core's default OPKGBUILDCMD has been 'opkg-build -Z zstd' since
honister, so every modern ipk carries data.tar.zst.  get_file_list()
only tries data.tar.gz and data.tar.xz, so opkg-make-index -l emits an
empty Packages.filelist and one "Package ... disappeared on us!"
warning per package.  Python's tarfile has no zstd support, so pipe the
member through the zstd tool.

Also send the "Lost field" message from read_control() to stderr:
without -p the index itself goes to stdout and the stray print corrupts
it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
---
--- a/opkg.py
+++ b/opkg.py
@@ -294,7 +294,9 @@
                 elif all_fields:
                     self.user_defined_fields[name] = value
                 else:
-                    print("Lost field %s, %s" % (name,value))
+                    # keep stdout clean: without -p the index itself goes to
+                    # stdout and a stray print corrupts it
+                    sys.stderr.write("Lost field %s, %s\n" % (name, value))
                     pass
 
                 if line and line[0] == '\n':
@@ -440,8 +442,24 @@
             tarStream = ar.open("data.tar.gz")
             tarf = tarfile.open("data.tar.gz", "r", tarStream)
         except IOError:
-            tarStream = ar.open("data.tar.xz")
-            tarf = tarfile.open("data.tar.xz", "r:xz", tarStream)
+            try:
+                tarStream = ar.open("data.tar.xz")
+                tarf = tarfile.open("data.tar.xz", "r:xz", tarStream)
+            except IOError:
+                # opkg-build -Z zstd (oe-core's default OPKGBUILDCMD since
+                # honister) produces data.tar.zst; Python's tarfile cannot
+                # read zstd, so decompress via the zstd tool.
+                import io
+                tarStream = ar.open("data.tar.zst")
+                compressed = tarStream.read(tarStream.size)
+                try:
+                    decomp = subprocess.run(["zstd", "-dc"], input=compressed,
+                                            stdout=subprocess.PIPE, check=True)
+                except (OSError, subprocess.CalledProcessError) as e:
+                    raise IOError("cannot decompress data.tar.zst from %s: %s"
+                                  % (self.fn, e))
+                tarf = tarfile.open("data.tar.zst", "r:",
+                                    fileobj=io.BytesIO(decomp.stdout))
         self.file_list = tarf.getnames()
         self.file_list = [["./", ""][a.startswith("./")] + a for a in self.file_list]
 
